        "h_title": "Executive Summary / Key Takeaways",
        "main_title": "2026 Travel Guide: Boonsiri Ferry Schedules, Routes, and Pricing (Gulf of Thailand & Eastern Coast)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Comprehensive Dual-Zone Network: Boonsiri Ferry (บริษัท บุญศิริเรือเร็ว จำกัด) operates seamlessly integrated land-and-sea transit routes connecting travelers to Koh Tao, Koh Phangan, and Koh Samui ( Southern Gulf Zone ), as well as Trat, Koh Kood, Koh Mak, and Koh Chang ( Eastern Coast Zone ).",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "2026 Premium Route Launch: Newly introduced daily **Direct Routes from Suvarnabhumi Airport (BKK)** link international arrivals straight to both marine zones without multi-provider transit hassle.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Unified Joint Tickets: Services run via VIP coaches synchronized with high-speed catamarans (featuring the new \"Boonsiri Sealine\" fleet in the Gulf zone) for a single-ticket, hassle-free check-in experience.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "June Low-Season Operational Advisory: Eastern routes (Trat to Koh Kood/Koh Mak/Koh Chang) are subject to weather-dependent schedule changes during the monsoon season. Pre-verification of fleet status is highly recommended.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
