      {
        "h_title": "💡 Industry Insights & Conversational FAQ",
        "main_title": "2026 Travel Guide: Boonsiri Ferry Schedules, Routes, and Pricing (Gulf of Thailand & Eastern Coast)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "First-Hand Ground Insight for June 2026 Travel:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "June marks the beginning of the Southwest Monsoon (Low Season) for the Eastern Gulf (Trat, Koh Kood, Koh Chang). While the Southern Gulf (Koh Tao, Samui) remains relatively sheltered during this period, weather conditions at sea can change abruptly. Boonsiri Ferry operates strictly under maritime safety protocols; therefore, certain vessel departures may be rescheduled, delayed, or swapped based on real-time sea conditions and passenger volume. Recommendation: When booking return trips to catch international flights, always factor in a minimum buffer window of 3 to 4 hours at the airport.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Q: What is the most efficient way to travel from Bangkok to Koh Kood?",
        "main_title": "2026 Travel Guide: Boonsiri Ferry Schedules, Routes, and Pricing (Gulf of Thailand & Eastern Coast)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "A: The most reliable and cost-effective option is the unified Joint Ticket departing from Khao San Road, Bangkok. Boonsiri Ferry provides three departures (05:00 AM, 06:00 AM, and 08:00 AM) that perfectly synchronize coach arrival times with ferry departures from Laem Sok Pier, eliminating the logistical risk of missing the boat transfer.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Q: How do I get to Koh Chang, Koh Mak, or Koh Kood straight from Suvarnabhumi Airport?",
        "main_title": "2026 Travel Guide: Boonsiri Ferry Schedules, Routes, and Pricing (Gulf of Thailand & Eastern Coast)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "A: You can utilize Boonsiri Ferry's Direct Route which departs from Suvarnabhumi Airport (BKK) daily at 09:00 AM. This service drives straight to Trat's piers, reaching Koh Chang by 02:00 PM, Koh Mak by 03:45 PM, and Koh Kood by 04:00 PM—making it ideal for passengers arriving on early morning flights.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
